  "name": "ICELAND-FAROE GAP",
  "description": "The Iceland-Faroe Ridge: 270 miles of shallow water between two coastlines, and the eastern half of the gap every Northern Fleet boat bound for the Atlantic has to cross. A Kilo is somewhere in it, running slow and deep on batteries. You have a Virginia holding the northern approach, a barrier force on the surface, and a Poseidon out of Keflavik with sixty buoys. Find it before it is through. Real geography and real platform families; the conflict, the deployment and the tactical situation are fiction.",
